  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485. Speeds 9600 to 115200 bit/s, even, odd or no parity. Holding the reset button sets address 1, 19200 bit/s and no parity temporarily; holding it for more than 10 seconds restores the factory data.",
    "The manual lists the registers as 40001 on with an offset column from 0; the map uses the offset, as sent on the wire. The register numbers named in the register-type tables (relay status 40003, baud rate 40009, parity 40010, input type 40012, retransmission 40075 and 40083) fix the order of the descriptions. The reserved rows after the alarm block are left out and the linearization table starts at offset 34, as the manual's offsets show.",
    "Values are signed 16-bit integers with the decimal places in register 17, in the range -30000 to +30000. Inputs: thermocouples J, K, T, R, S, E, N, B; Pt100 (2 or 3 wires); 0-20 and 4-20 mA; 0-100 mV, 0-5 V and 0-10 V; logic level; frequency 0.4 Hz to 30 kHz. A 4-20 mA signal below 3.5 mA is read as burn-out.",
    "The XM-102 has one analog output and the XM-112 two; the registers of output 2 exist only on the XM-112.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
